# Line endings (cadence.md §7.14, TD-187): every text file is LF in the repository and in every
# checkout, whatever a clone's core.autocrlf says. A file that must be CRLF says so below.
# SEED: the repo owns this file — add its own patterns, keep the first rule.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows scripts, run by cmd.exe or PowerShell, keep CRLF.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# The ledgerboard fixtures' bytes are what their tests check, CRLF and mixed endings included:
# git never converts them (TD-1913; agent-cadence's own seed uses the same rule).
tests/ledgerboard/** -text
